SCOPE

This MIT license covers the CODE in this repository: everything under `tools/`
(shell scripts, Python, C and assembly sources) and everything under
`.claude/hooks/`.

The DOCUMENTATION -- `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/`, `notes/`, `tools/README.md`
and the other Markdown files -- is licensed separately under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International. See LICENSE-docs.

ONE EXCEPTION, deliberately carved out: `tools/patches/` contains modifications
to third-party GPL-3.0 source (OptiScaler) and is licensed GPL-3.0, not MIT.
Nothing in that directory is required by, or linked into, anything else here.
See `tools/patches/README.md`.

WHY MIT

The probes in `tools/isa-probe/` and `tools/fex-tests/` exist to be handed
upstream as minimal reproducers for translator bugs. FEX-Emu and Box64 are both
MIT-licensed, so a maintainer can drop these sources straight into their own test
suite with no attribution machinery to carry. That mattered more here than the
patent grant a more elaborate license would add.
